                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have played QuiVR, Elven Assassin, the Lab (archery game), Deadly Hunter, and Twisted Arrow (I'm not including games that are not solely focused on Bow and arrow, such as Raw Data).  Out of all those archery games in VR, I had the most fun playing this game.  Not only are the graphics better in this game, but the gameplay is satisfying and challenging, without it being too frustrating.  Each level brings a higher difficulty and a new challenge.  I especially like how there's no teleporting around.  It just makes more sense.  If you're defending place, you usually pick the best spot to shoot arrows and stay there.  Yeah, I wish you could move at least a little, but it's better than teleporting all around the map.  \n\nI'm not going to write here about the physics or whether the bow and arrow is realistic, because I have never tried to hit moving targets with a bow and arrow.  The most I have done is mess around and try to hit a standing target at ground level.  I can tell you that the physics are predictable.  My only complaint is that I wish there was a little bit more feedback on the controller to tell when the arrow was pulled as far as it can go.  You mostly just get that from experience in playing the game.  \n\nI do recommend turning hands off.  Make sure you do the setup at the start of the game to get the right bow for you.  I also wish you could use a melee weapon when enemies charge at you.  Another thing is that I wish you could switch between a shield and a bow and arrow to add more challenge when projectiles are hurled your way (versus having to always shoot the projectiles).  But even as is, I had a blast playing this game.  I'm surprised this game hasn't gotten more positive reviews.  It's a real hidden gem.\n\nRating 8/10",
